From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:30:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fsgen: do not put vendor-only modules in the generated system
 image

A device with no separate vendor partition sets TARGET_COPY_OUT_VENDOR to
system/vendor, so PartitionTag() answers "system" for a module built only
as a vendor variant. collectDepsMutator then adds it to the generated
system image, which resolves its dependencies with the core variation, and
analysis fails:

  dependency "android.hardware.health-service.qti" of
  "lineage_<device>_generated_system_image" missing variant:
    os:android,arch:arm64_armv8-a
  available variants:
    os:android,image:vendor,arch:arm64_armv8-a

The mutator already has a list of variations that answer "system" without
belonging to it -- ramdisk, vendor_ramdisk and recovery, which cc/image.go
marks as platform. Vendor and product are the same situation for a device
laid out this way, so add them.

No effect where a vendor or product partition exists: there PartitionTag()
returns that partition, so the branch is never reached.

---
 fsgen/fsgen_mutators.go | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fsgen/fsgen_mutators.go b/fsgen/fsgen_mutators.go
index 080cb39dc..1eff37b66 100644
--- a/fsgen/fsgen_mutators.go
+++ b/fsgen/fsgen_mutators.go
@@ -454,6 +454,12 @@ func collectDepsMutator(mctx android.BottomUpMutatorContext) {
 			android.RamdiskVariation,
 			android.VendorRamdiskVariation,
 			android.RecoveryVariation,
+			// A device with no vendor or product partition installs that image inside
+			// /system, so PartitionTag() answers "system" for a module whose only
+			// variants are vendor or product ones. Adding it to the generated system
+			// image then asks for a core variant the module does not have.
+			android.VendorVariation,
+			android.ProductVariation,
 		})
 		if isEligibleForFsDeps(mctx) && !systemPartitionFalsePositive {
 			appendDepIfAppropriate(mctx, fsGenState.fsDeps[installPartition], installPartition, android.NativeBridgeDisabled, mctx.ModuleName())
